#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:7
msgid "Managing Dependencies with rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:11
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr "目次表"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:13
msgid "**Goal:** Manage external dependencies using ``rosdep``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:15
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr "**教學等級：** 中級"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:17
msgid "**Time:** 5 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:19
msgid ""
"This tutorial will explain how to manage external dependencies using "
"``rosdep``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:23
msgid ""
"Currently rosdep only works on Linux and macOS; Windows is not supported. "
"There are long-term plans to add support for Windows to https://github.com/"
"ros-infrastructure/rosdep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:27
msgid "What is rosdep?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:29
msgid ""
"``rosdep`` is a dependency management utility that can work with packages "
"and external libraries. It is a command-line utility for identifying and "
"installing dependencies to build or install a package. ``rosdep`` is *not* a "
"package manager in its own right; it is a meta-package manager that uses its "
"own knowledge of the system and the dependencies to find the appropriate "
"package to install on a particular platform. The actual installation is done "
"using the system package manager (e.g. ``apt`` on Debian/Ubuntu, ``dnf`` on "
"Fedora/RHEL, etc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:34
msgid ""
"It is most often invoked before building a workspace, where it is used to "
"install the dependencies of the packages within that workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:36
msgid ""
"It has the ability to work over a single package or over a directory of "
"packages (e.g. workspace)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:40
msgid ""
"While the name suggests it is for ROS, ``rosdep`` is semi-agnostic to ROS. "
"You can utilize this powerful tool in non-ROS software projects by "
"installing it as a standalone Python package. Successfully running "
"``rosdep`` relies on ``rosdep keys`` to be available, which can be "
"downloaded from a public git repository with a few simple commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:45
msgid "A little about package.xml files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:47
msgid ""
"The ``package.xml`` is the file in your software where ``rosdep`` finds the "
"set of dependencies. It is important that the list of dependencies in the "
"``package.xml`` is complete and correct, which allows all of the tooling to "
"determine the packages dependencies. Missing or incorrect dependencies can "
"lead to users not being able to use your package, to packages in a workspace "
"being built out-of-order, and to packages not being able to be released."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:51
msgid ""
"The dependencies in the ``package.xml`` file are generally referred to as "
"\"rosdep keys\". These dependencies are manually populated in the ``package."
"xml`` file by the package's creators and should be an exhaustive list of any "
"non-builtin libraries and packages it requires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:54
msgid ""
"These are represented in the following tags (see `REP-149 <https://reps."
"openrobotics.org/rep-0149/>`__ for the full specification):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:57
msgid "``<depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:59
msgid ""
"These are dependencies that should be provided at both build time and run "
"time for your package. For C++ packages, if in doubt, use this tag. Pure "
"Python packages generally don't have a build phase, so should never use this "
"and should use ``<exec_depend>`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:64
msgid "``<build_depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:66
msgid ""
"If you only use a particular dependency for building your package, and not "
"at execution time, you can use the ``<build_depend>`` tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:68
msgid ""
"With this type of dependency, an installed binary of your package does not "
"require that particular package to be installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:70
msgid ""
"However, that can create a problem if your package exports a header that "
"includes a header from this dependency. In that case you also need a "
"``<build_export_depend>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:74
msgid "``<build_export_depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:76
msgid ""
"If you export a header that includes a header from a dependency, it will be "
"needed by other packages that ``<build_depend>`` on yours. This mainly "
"applies to headers and CMake configuration files. Library packages "
"referenced by libraries you export should normally specify ``<depend>``, "
"because they are also needed at execution time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:81
msgid "``<exec_depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:83
msgid ""
"This tag declares dependencies for shared libraries, executables, Python "
"modules, launch scripts and other files required when running your package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:86
msgid "``<test_depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:88
msgid ""
"This tag declares dependencies needed only by tests. Dependencies here "
"should *not* be duplicated with keys specified by ``<build_depend>``, "
"``<exec_depend>``, or ``<depend>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:92
msgid "How does rosdep work?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:94
msgid ""
"``rosdep`` will check for ``package.xml`` files in its path or for a "
"specific package and find the rosdep keys stored within. These keys are then "
"cross-referenced against a central index to find the appropriate ROS package "
"or software library in various package managers. Finally, once the packages "
"are found, they are installed and ready to go!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:98
msgid ""
"``rosdep`` works by retrieving the central index on to your local machine so "
"that it doesn't have to access the network every time it runs (on Debian/"
"Ubuntu the configuration for it is stored in ``/etc/ros/rosdep/sources.list."
"d/20-default.list``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:100
msgid ""
"The central index is known as ``rosdistro``, which `may be found online "
"<https://github.com/ros/rosdistro>`_. We'll explore that more in the next "
"section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:104
msgid "How do I know what keys to put in my package.xml?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:106
msgid "Great question, I'm glad you asked!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:108
msgid ""
"If the package you want to depend in your package is ROS-based, AND has been "
"released into the ROS ecosystem [1]_, e.g. ``nav2_bt_navigator``, you may "
"simply use the name of the package. You can find a list of all released ROS "
"packages in https://github.com/ros/rosdistro at ``<distro>/distribution."
"yaml`` (e.g. ``humble/distribution.yaml``) for your given ROS distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:110
msgid ""
"If you want to depend on a non-ROS package, something often called \"system "
"dependencies\", you will need to find the keys for a particular library. In "
"general, there are two files of interest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:113
msgid ""
"`rosdep/base.yaml <https://github.com/ros/rosdistro/blob/master/rosdep/base."
"yaml>`_ contains the ``apt`` system dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:114
msgid ""
"`rosdep/python.yaml <https://github.com/ros/rosdistro/blob/master/rosdep/"
"python.yaml>`_ contains the Python dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:116
msgid ""
"To find a key, search for your library in these files and find the name. "
"This is the key to put in a ``package.xml`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:119
msgid ""
"For example, imagine a package had a dependency on ``doxygen`` because it is "
"a great piece of software that cares about quality documentation (hint "
"hint). We would search ``rosdep/base.yaml`` for ``doxygen`` and come across:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:122
msgid ""
"doxygen:\n"
"  arch: [doxygen]\n"
"  debian: [doxygen]\n"
"  fedora: [doxygen]\n"
"  freebsd: [doxygen]\n"
"  gentoo: [app-doc/doxygen]\n"
"  macports: [doxygen]\n"
"  nixos: [doxygen]\n"
"  openembedded: [doxygen@meta-oe]\n"
"  opensuse: [doxygen]\n"
"  rhel: [doxygen]\n"
"  ubuntu: [doxygen]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:137
msgid ""
"That means our rosdep key is ``doxygen``, which would resolve to those "
"various names in different operating system's package managers for "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:140
msgid "What if my library isn't in rosdistro?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:142
msgid ""
"If your library isn't in ``rosdistro``, you can experience the greatness "
"that is open-source software development: you can add it yourself! Pull "
"requests for rosdistro are typically merged well within a week."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:145
msgid ""
"`Detailed instructions may be found here <https://github.com/ros/rosdistro/"
"blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#rosdep-rules-contributions>`_ for how to "
"contribute new rosdep keys. If for some reason these may not be contributed "
"openly, other options exist:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:148
msgid ""
"Forking rosdistro and maintaining a alternate index containing the extra "
"keys (:doc:`../../../Migration-and-Upgrades/Using-Custom-Rosdistro`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:149
msgid ""
"Creating a new file containing custom keys and instructing ``rosdep`` to "
"check it when populating the local index (:doc:`../../../Developer-Tools/"
"Build/Supplementing-Custom-Rosdep-Keys`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:152
msgid "How do I use the rosdep tool?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:155
msgid "rosdep installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:157
msgid ""
"If you are using ``rosdep`` with ROS, it is conveniently packaged along with "
"the ROS distribution. This is the recommended way to get ``rosdep``. You can "
"install it with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:163
msgid "Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:165
msgid "$ sudo apt install python3-rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:169
msgid "RHEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:171
msgid "$ sudo dnf install python3-rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:177
msgid ""
"On Debian and Ubuntu, there is another, similarly named package called "
"``python3-rosdep2``. If that package is installed, make sure to remove it "
"before installing ``python3-rosdep``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:180
msgid ""
"If you are using ``rosdep`` outside of ROS, the system package may not be "
"available. In that case, you can install it directly from https://pypi.org:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:183
msgid "$ pip install rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:188
msgid "rosdep operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:190
msgid ""
"Now that we have some understanding of ``rosdep``, ``package.xml``, and "
"``rosdistro``, we're ready to use the utility itself! Firstly, if this is "
"the first time using ``rosdep``, it must be initialized via:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:193
msgid ""
"$ sudo rosdep init\n"
"$ rosdep update"
msgstr ""
"$ sudo rosdep init\n"
"$ rosdep update"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:198
msgid ""
"This will initialize rosdep and ``update`` will update the locally cached "
"rosdistro index. It is a good idea to ``update`` rosdep on occasion to get "
"the latest index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:201
msgid ""
"Finally, we can run ``rosdep install`` to install dependencies. Typically, "
"this is run over a workspace with many packages in a single call to install "
"all dependencies. A call for that would appear as the following, if in the "
"root of the workspace with directory ``src`` containing source code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:205
msgid "$ rosdep install --from-paths src -y --ignore-src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:209
msgid "Breaking that down:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:211
msgid ""
"``--from-paths src`` specifies the path to check for ``package.xml`` files "
"to resolve keys for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:212
msgid ""
"``-y`` means to default yes to all prompts from the package manager to "
"install without prompts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:213
msgid ""
"``--ignore-src`` means to ignore installing dependencies, even if a rosdep "
"key exists, if the package itself is also in the workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:215
msgid ""
"There are additional arguments and options available. Use ``rosdep -h`` to "
"see them, or look at the more complete documentation for rosdep at http://"
"docs.ros.org/en/independent/api/rosdep/html/ ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Rosdep.rst:218
msgid ""
"\"released into the ROS ecosystem\" means the package is listed in one or "
"more of the ``<distro>/distribution.yaml`` directories in the `rosdistro "
"database <https://github.com/ros/rosdistro>`_."
msgstr ""
